OpenWings patch 0008: browser automation through the OpenWings browser container

Upstream ships the private_browser tool, its schema and the agent-side
plumbing, but this build answers every page action with UNSUPPORTED. With
the browser compose profile on, OpenWings routes those actions to
wings/browser.py, which drives a headful Chromium in the browser container
over the DevTools protocol (Playwright) and returns each page as a numbered
outline the model acts on by ref.

  * src/tool_execution.py: page actions go to wings.browser.run() when the
    OpenWings browser is enabled; otherwise upstream behaviour is unchanged.
  * src/agent_runtime/authority.py: a browser task may click, fill and press
    without repeating each verb in the request. The backend itself hands
    passwords, one-time codes, card numbers and pay/order/send/publish/delete
    clicks to the person, and blocks private addresses and non-web schemes.
  * routes/chat_routes.py: everyday web-task wording (sign in to a portal,
    book or order online, fill in a form, add to cart) routes to the browser.
  * src/agent_loop.py: older page outlines are dropped from the context when a
    newer one arrives; page text the agent read is kept.
  * src/tool_schemas.py, src/tool_index.py: describe what the tool does now.
  * src/settings.py: agent_max_rounds defaults to 40 (was 20); web tasks take
    many small steps. Settings > Agent still controls it.
  * app.py: mounts the live view routes (wings/browser_routes.py).
    scripts/verify_frontend_runtime.py copies the wings package into its
    isolated distribution check, since app.py now imports it.
  * static/js/wings-ui.js: a "Live browser" sidebar entry, shown only when
    the browser is enabled and the account may use it.

